comments.content:
**Maintainability: Silent key-resolution failures produce `NO-KEY` ledger entries with no logging or metrics.**

When `getOpenRouterKey()` or `getNvidiaKey()` throws (e.g., file missing, malformed JSON), the `catch { return ''; }` swallows the error entirely. `runScanChain` then logs `NO-KEY` to the ledger (line 229), but there is no `console.warn`, metric counter, or any other signal. If the auth file is corrupted or missing, the operator has no visibility into why the OpenRouter and NVIDIA rungs are being silently skipped — the chain just falls through with zero useful diagnostics.

**Fix:** At minimum, log the error on key resolution failure:
```typescript
} catch (e) {
  console.warn('[scan-chain] Failed to resolve OpenRouter key:', e);
  return '';
}
```

