comments.content:
The component-lookup-and-requireUp pattern is duplicated three times across the two layers (lines 109–116 for ABIDE/JEV, lines 195–198 for TSG, lines 245–250 for JEV). Each instance follows the same sequence: `register.find(id) → null-check with named Error → requireUp`. Extract a small helper, e.g.:
```typescript
function requireComponent(deps: EnforcementDeps, id: string, code: string): void {
  const decl = deps.register.find((c) => c.id === id);
  if (!decl) throw Object.assign(new Error(`${id} is not registered`), { code });
  requireUp(decl);
}
```
This eliminates the three near-identical try-catch-guard blocks and reduces the surface area for future inconsistencies (e.g. mismatched codes between the find-guard and the catch fallback, which was the exact class of bug fixed in F-530).

